      "created_at": "2018-09-11T12:09:47Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-09-11T12:09:47Z",
      "body": "Thanks for creating the issue.\r\nI like the idea of having the abstraction with an analytics service.\r\n\r\nI briefly checked Heap and one thing we'll need to add is an identification `heap.identify(userId)` of the installation. I think we can do this with an uuid that we'll generate on first start because electronStore will not contain that id or do we have another option to do this because clearing the store would always create a new userId?\r\nBut I think that's the easiest way with-out a login and probably won't happen often. Or maybe we can read an id from the computer (e.g. network MAC address) and use this as identifier.\r\n\r\nA location to store the id would be in an `analytics.reducer` or maybe we could add an `app-settings.reducer` and store the Id there. So we can also add app settings there later e.g. author name, E-Mail etc.",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "pin": null,
